Original commit body from c1aa72a471f80815c1aa46e41b97618b2ebfbbf9:

Every run now folds its per-test coverage into a persistent block -> tests
index; a shadow reporter says what a coverage-driven selector WOULD have
chosen and acts on none of it. Nothing about test selection changes yet.

Keyed on AST-block digests, not line numbers: an insertion above a function
must not look like a change to it. Children are removed from a parent's
digest entirely rather than left as name markers -- the marker design made
every structural edit perturb the enclosing block, and a module-level def's
parent is import-time code credited to EVERY test in the file, so adding one
function selected the whole suite. Renames and moves are caught by the
vanished-key rule instead. A block owns its BODY, not its `def` header,
because the header executes at import in the enclosing scope.

FOURTH selector, not a replacement. Coverage beats the import-graph slice on
packages/*/src, loses to top_level_test_map on scripts/ (subprocess tests
leave no in-process trace), and cannot see YAML or fixtures. Unioned, never
subtracted, and local only -- CI keeps running everything.

Three defects found end-to-end, all green at unit level:
  - change detection was measured against the INDEX, which is rewritten every
    run, so the baseline advanced and run 2 compared the tree against itself:
    0 selected vs smart-test's 87. It belongs to git.
  - the targeted path scopes --cov to changed files, so "ran and produced
    nothing" marked 1,507 of 1,662 tests unmeasured -- and unmeasured tests
    are excluded from selection, making most of the suite unselectable.
  - a cold index reports every test as a miss while looking trustworthy;
    those observations are now excluded rather than poisoning the evidence.

Also fixes two one-fact-two-homes drifts in smart-test itself: COV_PATHS is
rebuilt on the targeted path (dropping --cov-context), and --full exits
before the index update. Both now route through one definition.

Demonstrated: one function changed in edge_types.py selects 12 tests across
2 files out of 22,801, including a runtime dependency in test_cli_explain.py.

Full suite green: 22,801 passed, 100% coverage. ruff/bandit/mypy ratchet clean.

